@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text.Json
@using MerkaiTrial.Application.Configuration
@model MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages.Quotes.QuoteItemsEditorVm
@{
    var hasCatalog = Model.Products is { Count: > 0 };

    // 052. The unit dropdown is built ONCE here, server side, and the script
    // clones it for every row. Building it in JavaScript would mean the unit
    // list existing twice — as C# constants and as a JS array — which is the
    // duplication ProductCatalog.cs was written to remove.
    //
    // Escaped with JsonSerializer, not string concatenation: a label is
    // server data going into a script block, and "Unit / piece" is harmless
    // only until someone adds a unit with an apostrophe in it.
    var unitGroups = UnitsOfMeasure.Grouped()
        .Select(g => new
        {
            group = g.Key,
            units = g.Select(u => new { code = u.Code, label = u.Label }).ToList()
        })
        .ToList();

    // 067. The tax classification code — HSN / SAC in India, "Tax code"
    // everywhere else. The short form, because this one goes in a cell of a
    // table that already has seven columns, not on a product form with a
    // label above it. TaxCodes is the one place the wording lives, so the
    // product form, this editor, both detail pages and both PDFs all say
    // the same thing.
    var taxCodeLabel = TaxCodes.ColumnHeaderFor(Model.CurrencyCode);
    var taxCodeMax   = TaxCodes.MaxLength;
}
@* =====================================================================
   _QuoteItemsEditor.cshtml
   Location: MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web/Pages/Quotes/_QuoteItemsEditor.cshtml

   NEW FILE (029) — the one line-item editor, rendered by both
   Create.cshtml and Edit.cshtml. QuoteItemsEditorVm.cs says why it exists
   and what went wrong with two copies.

   IT MUST BE RENDERED INSIDE THE FORM it posts with: it owns the hidden
   itemsJson field, and the host page owns the form, the dates and the
   buttons.

   ── 067: A TAX CLASSIFICATION CODE PER LINE ─────────────────────────

   Products have carried a tax code since 051 — HSN / SAC in India — and
   it stopped at the product. The quote line had no field for it, so the
   invoice raised from the quote had none either, and the one document
   that legally has to print it could not.

   The box sits beside the description rather than in a column of its
   own: the table already has seven columns and the numeric ones cannot
   wrap, while the description can. It is editable, not read-only from
   the catalogue, for one case a product-only snapshot misses entirely —
   a CUSTOM line, typed by hand with no product behind it, still needs a
   code on an Indian invoice.

   Picking a product from the catalogue fills the box in from
   data-taxcode, the same way it fills in the unit. Clearing the box
   clears the code: the editor always POSTS the field, and the server
   reads "" as "deliberately empty" and null as "nothing to say, ask the
   product" — see LineTaxCodes.Resolve. Those two being different is
   what makes the box clearable at all.

   ── 052: DECIMAL QUANTITY, AND A UNIT PER LINE ──────────────────────

   The quantity box was min="1" step="1" with a whole-number check behind
   it, so the editor could not express most of what Merkai's customers
   sell: 12.5 m² of flooring, 3.5 consulting days, 0.75 kg of freight.
   What people did instead was put the real quantity in the description
   and fudge the unit price until the line total came out right — which
   makes the TOTAL correct and every report about WHAT was sold wrong.

   Three changes:

   1. The box is now step="any" min="0" and accepts decimals. The only
      rule left is that a line must be for something (> 0), enforced here
      AND by QuoteLineChecks on the API.

   2. Every row carries a UNIT — a dropdown under the number, built from
      UnitsOfMeasure. A line added from the catalogue arrives with the
      product's own unit already chosen (data-unit), so in the normal case
      nobody touches it.

   3. Quantities are rounded to 4 decimal places AS THEY ARE TYPED, not
      only on submit. The column is DECIMAL(18,4), and SQL Server rounds
      anything finer silently — a quantity of 0.00004 would have become
      0.0000 and the line would have priced at nothing. Now the zero shows
      up on screen, where somebody can see it.

   The unit list is serialised from UnitsOfMeasure rather than written out
   again as a JavaScript array, so there is one definition of what a unit
   is. A line carrying a code this build does not recognise keeps it, in
   its own "On this line" group, instead of being quietly re-labelled the
   moment somebody opens the quote.

   ── 055: A DISCOUNT CAN BE A PERCENTAGE ─────────────────────────────

   The discount box only ever took an AMOUNT. Reps do not sell that way —
   they agree "10% off" and work out what that is on a calculator, line by
   line, and type the answer in. Every one of those is a chance to put a
   wrong figure on a document a customer signs.

   Each line now has a small selector under the discount box: the tenant's
   currency, or %. In % mode the box holds the percentage and the amount is
   derived on every keystroke; in amount mode it holds the amount, as
   before. Switching between them CONVERTS rather than resetting, so
   flipping to % to check a figure does not wipe it.

   Both are posted. The SERVER recomputes the amount from the percentage
   and ignores the one the browser sent — see LineDiscounts.cs. That is not
   distrust of this file; it is that the API is public, and a request
   carrying "10%" with an amount of zero must not produce a line at full
   price wearing a 10% badge.

   WHAT THIS FIXES, beyond removing the duplication

   1. NONE OF THE VALIDATION ON THE OLD PAGES EVER RAN. Every input had
      required / min="1" / max="100" on it, and both pages submitted with
      form.submit() — which by specification skips HTML5 constraint
      validation AND the submit event. So a quantity of 0, a 500% tax rate
      and a negative discount all went to the server, and the page looked
      like it was validating. Validation is now done in JS before
      submitting, marks the offending cell, and lists what's wrong; the
      API is still the real gate.

   2. TYPED VALUES COULD BE LOST. The old syncLineItemsFromUI() copied only
      name and description out of the DOM; qty, price, tax and discount
      lived in the array and were only ever updated by an oninput handler.
      Anything that changes an input's value without firing `input` — and a
      few browser autofill paths don't — was silently dropped on submit.
      Every input now has an id and syncFromDom() re-reads all six.

   3. THE DISCOUNT ROW COULD CONTRADICT THE GRAND TOTAL. Per-line discount
      was clamped to the line subtotal for the tax calculation but NOT when
      summing the Discount row, so a discount bigger than the line showed a
      Discount larger than the Subtotal with a Grand Total of 0. The clamp
      is applied once, in one place, and the input's own max follows the
      line.

   4. NO INLINE onclick / oninput ANYWHERE. Everything is delegated
      listeners plus data- attributes, so no product name, description or
      quantity is ever interpolated into a JavaScript string. That is what
      broke the Edit page's catalogue on a product named  Widget "Pro".

   5. THE REMOVE CONTROL WAS AN <i> WITH AN onclick. Not focusable, not
      reachable by keyboard, no accessible name. It is a <button> now.

   ── 050 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   6. THE PRODUCT'S TAX RATE WAS IGNORED. Picking a product from the
      catalogue set the line's tax to the WORKSPACE default, never the
      product's own:

          taxRate: num(DEFAULT_TAX, 0)

      and the product buttons carried no tax attribute to read. So
      Product.TaxRate was decorative: a 5% product in a 7% workspace
      produced a 7% line, on the quote and on every invoice raised from
      it. Nothing anywhere said so.

      The rate now travels with the product, and the catalogue shows it
      beside the price so a rate that differs from the default is visible
      before the line is added.

      An UNSET rate still inherits the workspace default; a rate set to
      ZERO stays zero, because a tax-exempt product is a real thing and
      must not quietly pick up the default.
   ===================================================================== *@

<style>
    .qe-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: .6rem; }
    .qe-head h2 { font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #64748b;
                  font-weight: 650; margin: 0; }
    .qe-head .sp { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: .4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

    .qe-shell { border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; overflow: hidden; }
    .qe-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0; }
    .qe-table th { font-size: .68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #64748b;
                   font-weight: 650; padding: .5rem .5rem; background: #fbfcfd;
                   border-bottom: 1px solid #eceff2; white-space: nowrap; }
    .qe-table td { padding: .4rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #f4f6f8; vertical-align: top; }
    .qe-table tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
    .qe-table .form-control, .qe-table .form-select { font-size: .84rem; }
    .qe-table input[type="number"] { text-align: right; }

    /* 052. The Qty cell holds a number and a unit now. The select is
       deliberately quieter than the number — the quantity is what people
       read, the unit is what makes it mean something. */
    .qe-uom { font-size: .74rem !important; padding: .1rem .35rem; margin-top: .15rem;
              color: #475569; background: #fbfcfd; }
    .qe-uom:focus { color: #0f172a; background: #fff; }

    /* 055. The discount mode selector. Same quiet treatment as the unit
       selector — the number is what people read, the mode is what makes it
       mean something. */
    .qe-dmode { font-size: .74rem !important; padding: .1rem .35rem; margin-top: .15rem;
                color: #475569; background: #fbfcfd; }
    .qe-dmode:focus { color: #0f172a; background: #fff; }
    .qe-dmode.pct { color: #0d6efd; font-weight: 650; }

    /* 067. The tax-code box sits beside the description, not in a column of
       its own: the table already carries seven columns and an eighth would
       squeeze the numeric ones, which cannot wrap. Narrow, quiet, and
       monospaced so an eight-digit HSN stays readable at this size.

       flex-basis on the description rather than a width on the code box, so
       the code keeps its 7.5rem on a narrow screen and the description —
       the one thing here that CAN wrap — gives up the space. */
    .qe-item-row { display: flex; gap: .3rem; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: .25rem; }
    .qe-item-row > .qe-desc-wrap { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
    .qe-taxcode { flex: 0 0 7.5rem; font-size: .74rem !important; padding: .25rem .4rem;
                  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
                  color: #475569; background: #fbfcfd; text-align: left !important; }
    .qe-taxcode:focus { color: #0f172a; background: #fff; }
    .qe-taxcode::placeholder { font-family: inherit; color: #9aa6b2; }
    .qe-n { text-align: right; }
    .qe-row-no { color: #94a3b8; font-size: .8rem; padding-top: .8rem !important; }
    .qe-line-total { font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap; padding-top: .8rem !important; }
    .qe-pct { font-size: .7rem; color: #94a3b8; display: block; margin-top: .15rem; text-align: right; }
    .qe-pct.over { color: #b45309; font-weight: 650; }
    .qe-over td { background: #fff8f1; }
    .qe-rm { --bs-btn-padding-y: .15rem; --bs-btn-padding-x: .4rem; }

    .qe-empty { padding: 1.6rem 1rem; text-align: center; color: #94a3b8; font-size: .86rem; }
    .qe-empty i { font-size: 1.8rem; color: #d7dde3; display: block; margin-bottom: .4rem; }

    .qe-problems { border: 1px solid #f5c2c7; border-left: 5px solid #dc3545; border-radius: 10px;
                   background: #fff5f5; padding: .7rem 1rem; margin-top: .75rem; }
    .qe-problems ul { margin: .3rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .86rem; }

    .qe-hint { border: 1px solid #fed7aa; border-left: 5px solid #fd7e14; border-radius: 10px;
               background: #fff7ed; padding: .7rem 1rem; margin-top: .75rem; }
    .qe-hint ul { margin: .3rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .86rem; }
    .qe-hint .ft { font-size: .78rem; color: #64748b; margin-top: .35rem; }

    .qe-tot { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: .3rem .9rem; font-size: .9rem; }
    .qe-tot .lbl { color: #64748b; }
    .qe-tot .amt { text-align: right; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
    .qe-tot .rule { grid-column: 1 / -1; border-top: 1px solid #e5e8ec; margin: .3rem 0 .1rem; }
    .qe-tot .big { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; }

    .qe-prod { cursor: pointer; }
    .qe-prod .pn { font-weight: 600; font-size: .9rem; }
    .qe-prod .pd { font-size: .8rem; color: #64748b; }

    /* Stack the table into cards on a phone. A 7-column editor with number
       inputs in it is unusable at 390px wide otherwise. */
    @@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
        .qe-table thead { display: none; }
        .qe-table, .qe-table tbody, .qe-table tr, .qe-table td { display: block; width: 100%; }
        .qe-table tr { border-bottom: 1px solid #eceff2; padding: .5rem .25rem; }
        .qe-table td { border: 0; padding: .25rem .5rem; }
        .qe-table td[data-lbl]::before { content: attr(data-lbl); display: block; font-size: .66rem;
            text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 650;
            margin-bottom: .1rem; }
        .qe-row-no, .qe-line-total { padding-top: .25rem !important; }
        .qe-line-total { text-align: right; }
    }
</style>

@* The hidden field the host form posts. Named itemsJson on both pages
   because both handlers take `string itemsJson`. *@
<input type="hidden" name="itemsJson" id="qeItemsJson" />

<div class="qe-head">
    <h2><i class="bi bi-list-ul me-1"></i>Line items</h2>
    <div class="sp">
        @if (hasCatalog)
        {
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" id="qeOpenCatalog">
                <i class="bi bi-box-seam me-1"></i>Add from catalogue
            </button>
        }
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" id="qeAddLine">
            <i class="bi bi-plus-lg me-1"></i>Add line
        </button>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="qe-shell">
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="qe-table" id="qeTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width:2rem;">#</th>
                    <th>Item</th>
                    @* 052: wider, because the cell carries the unit as well now.
                       9rem rather than something tighter for a dull reason: a
                       closed <select> clips its own text and cannot be made to
                       ellipsize reliably, so "Square metre" has to FIT or the
                       chosen unit becomes unreadable. The table lives inside
                       .table-responsive, so the extra width costs a scrollbar
                       at worst. *@
                    <th style="width:9rem;" class="qe-n">Qty</th>
                    <th style="width:8rem;" class="qe-n">Unit price</th>
                    @* 055: wider — the cell carries the amount/% selector now. *@
                    <th style="width:9rem;" class="qe-n">Discount</th>
                    <th style="width:6rem;" class="qe-n">@Model.TaxLabel %</th>
                    <th style="width:8.5rem;" class="qe-n">Line total</th>
                    <th style="width:2.5rem;"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="qeBody"></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="qe-empty" id="qeEmpty">
        <i class="bi bi-inbox"></i>
        <div>No lines yet.</div>
        <div class="small">Add a line, or pick something from the catalogue.</div>
    </div>
</div>

@* Validation summary. Replaces three alert() calls — an alert cannot tell
   you WHICH line is wrong, and on a ten-line quote that matters. *@
<div class="qe-problems d-none" id="qeProblems" role="alert">
    <div class="fw-semibold"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>Fix these before saving</div>
    <ul id="qeProblemList"></ul>
</div>

@* (017) Live approval hint — the API enforces the same rules; this only
   tells the rep before they click. *@
<div class="qe-hint d-none" id="qeHint">
    <div class="fw-semibold">
        <i class="bi bi-shield-exclamation me-1" style="color:#fd7e14"></i>
        <span id="qeHintTitle">This quote will need approval</span>
    </div>
    <ul id="qeHintList"></ul>
    <div class="ft" id="qeHintFoot"></div>
</div>

<div class="row justify-content-end mt-3">
    <div class="col-sm-8 col-md-6 col-lg-5">
        <div class="qe-tot">
            <div class="lbl">Subtotal</div>
            <div class="amt" id="qeSubtotal">—</div>

            <div class="lbl">Discount</div>
            <div class="amt" id="qeDiscount">—</div>

            <div class="lbl">@Model.TaxLabel</div>
            <div class="amt" id="qeTax">—</div>

            <div class="rule"></div>

            <div class="lbl big">Grand total</div>
            <div class="amt big" id="qeGrand">—</div>
        </div>
        <div class="text-muted mt-1" style="font-size:.74rem;">
            Amounts in <strong>@Model.CurrencyCode</strong>. The server recalculates
            every total when you save.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@if (hasCatalog)
{
    <div class="modal fade" id="qeCatalog" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="qeCatalogTitle">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h5 class="modal-title" id="qeCatalogTitle">
                        <i class="bi bi-box-seam me-2"></i>Product catalogue
                    </h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <div class="input-group input-group-sm mb-3">
                        <span class="input-group-text"><i class="bi bi-search"></i></span>
                        <input type="search" class="form-control" id="qeProdSearch"
                               placeholder="Search by name or description" autocomplete="off"
                               aria-label="Search the product catalogue" />
                    </div>

                    <div class="list-group" id="qeProdList">
                        @foreach (var p in Model.Products)
                        {
                            @* 052: "/ m²", "/ hrs" — empty for a plain unit, because
                               "1,200.00 / units" reads worse than "1,200.00". *@
                            var perUnit = UnitsOfMeasure.ShortOf(p.UnitOfMeasure);

                            @* 067: shown in the list, because a rep picking
                               between two similar products in India may be
                               picking between two HSN codes, and a missing
                               code is something to notice BEFORE the line is
                               on the quote rather than after the invoice has
                               gone out. *@
                            var prodTaxCode = TaxCodes.Normalise(p.TaxCode);

                            @* Everything the click needs is in data- attributes, which
                               Razor HTML-encodes. Nothing is interpolated into a JS
                               string, so a product called  Widget "Pro"  or  Bob's Kit
                               is just data. The old Edit page built this with
                               Html.Raw(name.Replace("'","\\'")) inside a double-quoted
                               onclick, which a double quote in the name broke open —
                               and a null name crashed the page outright. *@
                            <button type="button" class="list-group-item list-group-item-action qe-prod"
                                    data-id="@p.Id"
                                    data-name="@(p.Name ?? string.Empty)"
                                    data-desc="@(p.Description ?? string.Empty)"
                                    @* 069: EMPTY when this product has no price in the
                                       quote's currency, which is a different thing from a
                                       price of zero and is read as such by the click
                                       handler. Sending the number anyway would be the
                                       defect this round fixes: a USD quote filled in from
                                       rupee figures. *@
                                    data-price="@(p.HasPriceInCurrency ? p.ListPrice.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : string.Empty)"
                                    data-tax="@(p.TaxRate?.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) ?? string.Empty)"
                                    @* 052: the product's own unit, snapshotted onto the line the
                                       moment it is added. Normalise() here rather than trusting
                                       the column, so a row written before 051 — or one carrying a
                                       code nobody recognises — still yields a usable unit. *@
                                    data-unit="@UnitsOfMeasure.Normalise(p.UnitOfMeasure)"
                                    @* 067: the product's tax classification code,
                                       snapshotted onto the line the same way. Through
                                       Normalise() so a code stored with stray spaces
                                       before this round does not travel onto a quote
                                       with them. *@
                                    data-taxcode="@(TaxCodes.Normalise(p.TaxCode) ?? string.Empty)"
                                    @* 070: the bundle's contents as ONE SENTENCE,
                                       built server-side by
                                       ProductBundles.BuildBreakdown. Dropped into the
                                       line's DESCRIPTION when the bundle is picked, so
                                       the quote keeps saying what the package contained
                                       on the day it went out even if the bundle is
                                       edited afterwards.

                                       Empty for every kind other than Bundle, which is
                                       how the click handler tells the two apart. Razor
                                       HTML-encodes it, so a component called
                                       Widget "Pro" is just data — the same rule 029 set
                                       for every other attribute on this button. *@
                                    data-bundle="@(p.BundleBreakdown ?? string.Empty)">
                                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-3">
                                    <div style="min-width:0;">
                                        <div class="pn">
                                            @(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.Name) ? "(unnamed product)" : p.Name)
                                            @if (p.IsBundle)
                                            {
                                                @* 070: so a rep can see it is a package
                                                   before they add it — the line that
                                                   arrives will carry a long description
                                                   they did not type, and that should not
                                                   be a surprise. *@
                                                <span class="badge bg-primary-subtle text-primary-emphasis border border-primary-subtle ms-1"
                                                      title="A bundle of @p.BundleComponentCount products. Added as one line with its contents listed.">
                                                    <i class="bi bi-boxes me-1"></i>Bundle
                                                </span>
                                            }
                                        </div>
                                        @if (p.IsBundle && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.BundleBreakdown))
                                        {
                                            <div class="pd fst-italic">@p.BundleBreakdown</div>
                                        }
                                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.Description))
                                        {
                                            <div class="pd">@p.Description</div>
                                        }
                                        @if (prodTaxCode is not null)
                                        {
                                            <div class="pd mt-1">
                                                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border fw-normal">
                                                    @taxCodeLabel @prodTaxCode
                                                </span>
                                            </div>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                    @* 050: the rate is shown as well as the price,
                                       because it is now what the line will actually
                                       use. A rate that silently differs from the
                                       workspace default is exactly the thing someone
                                       needs to see BEFORE they add the line. *@
                                    <div class="text-end flex-shrink-0">
                                        @* 069: a product with no price in THIS QUOTE'S
                                           currency says so instead of showing a figure.
                                           Still pickable — a rep may well know the price
                                           and type it — and the line then starts at zero,
                                           where the editor's own "needs a unit price above
                                           zero" check stops the save until they do. *@
                                        @if (p.HasPriceInCurrency)
                                        {
                                            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border">
                                                @Model.CurrencyCode @p.ListPrice.ToString("N2", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(perUnit) ? "" : " / " + perUnit)
                                            </span>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning-emphasis border border-warning-subtle"
                                                  title="This product has no @Model.CurrencyCode price. Add one under Products, or type the price on the line.">
                                                <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>No @Model.CurrencyCode price
                                            </span>
                                        }
                                        @if (p.TaxRate.HasValue)
                                        {
                                            <div class="pd mt-1">
                                                @Model.TaxLabel @p.TaxRate.Value.ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)%
                                            </div>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <div class="pd mt-1 fst-italic">
                                                @Model.TaxLabel @Model.DefaultTaxRate.ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)% (default)
                                            </div>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="qe-empty d-none" id="qeProdNone">
                        <i class="bi bi-search"></i>
                        <div>Nothing matches that.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@* Bootstrap JS is loaded once by _Layout.cshtml — not loaded again here. *@
<script>
    (function () {
        'use strict';

        // ── configuration from the server ────────────────────────────
        var DEFAULT_TAX = @Model.DefaultTaxRate.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        var RULES       = @Html.Raw(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.ApprovalRulesJson) ? "{\"enabled\":false}" : Model.ApprovalRulesJson);
        var LIST_PRICES = @Html.Raw(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.ListPricesJson) ? "{}" : Model.ListPricesJson);
        var SEED        = @Html.Raw(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.InitialItemsJson) ? "[]" : Model.InitialItemsJson);

        // 052. The unit list, straight from UnitsOfMeasure — one definition,
        // serialised, not a second copy written out in JavaScript.
        var UNIT_GROUPS  = @Html.Raw(JsonSerializer.Serialize(unitGroups));
        var DEFAULT_UNIT = @Html.Raw(JsonSerializer.Serialize(UnitsOfMeasure.Unit));

        // 067. The label and the length limit, serialised rather than
        // written out as a JS literal, for the same reason the unit list is:
        // TaxCodes decides the wording and the column width is NVARCHAR(20),
        // and neither should have a second definition in here to drift.
        var TAX_CODE_LABEL = @Html.Raw(JsonSerializer.Serialize(taxCodeLabel));
        var TAX_CODE_MAX   = @taxCodeMax;
        // Matches QuoteLineChecks.QuantityDecimals. The column is
        // DECIMAL(18,4): anything finer would be rounded by SQL Server
        // without a word, so 0.00004 would price at nothing.
        var QTY_DP = 4;

        // 055. What to call "an amount" in the discount selector. The
        // tenant's ISO code rather than a symbol: "INR" is unambiguous at
        // 11px, where a currency symbol beside a percent sign is not.
        var CCY    = @Html.Raw(JsonSerializer.Serialize(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.CurrencyCode) ? "Amount" : Model.CurrencyCode));
        var PCT_DP = 2;   // matches LineDiscounts.PercentDecimals
        var SEED_BLANK  = @(Model.StartWithOneBlankLine ? "true" : "false");
        var FORM_ID     = '@Model.FormId';

        // ── money ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        // MerkaiCurrency comes from _Layout and uses Intl.NumberFormat with
        // the tenant's culture, so the client and the server agree. If the
        // layout ever stops providing it, fall back rather than throwing on
        // every keystroke.
        function money(x) {
            var n = Number(x) || 0;
            try {
                if (window.MerkaiCurrency && typeof window.MerkaiCurrency.format === 'function') {
                    return window.MerkaiCurrency.format(n);
                }
            } catch (e) { /* fall through */ }
            return n.toFixed(2);
        }

        var body     = document.getElementById('qeBody');
        var emptyEl  = document.getElementById('qeEmpty');
        var jsonEl   = document.getElementById('qeItemsJson');
        if (!body || !jsonEl) return;

        var rows = [];      // the model
        var uid  = 1;       // DOM key, never sent to the server

        function num(v, fallback) {
            var n = parseFloat(v);
            return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : (fallback || 0);
        }

        // 052. A quantity, at the precision the column can actually hold.
        // Applied when reading the box, not only on submit, so the totals on
        // screen are the totals the server will store — typing 0.00004 shows
        // you a zero-quantity line here instead of surprising you with one
        // after saving.
        function qty(v, fallback) {
            var n = num(v, fallback);
            var f = Math.pow(10, QTY_DP);
            return Math.round(n * f) / f;
        }

        // 052. The unit dropdown for one row. Built from UNIT_GROUPS, so the
        // options come from UnitsOfMeasure and nowhere else.
        function unitSelect(k, code, lineNo) {
            var html = '<select class="form-select form-select-sm qe-uom" id="qe-uom-' + k + '"' +
                       ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="unitOfMeasure"' +
                       ' aria-label="Unit, line ' + lineNo + '">';

            var chosen = String(code || DEFAULT_UNIT);
            var matched = false;

            for (var g = 0; g < UNIT_GROUPS.length; g++) {
                html += '<optgroup label="' + esc(UNIT_GROUPS[g].group) + '">';
                var us = UNIT_GROUPS[g].units;
                for (var u = 0; u < us.length; u++) {
                    var sel = (us[u].code === chosen);
                    if (sel) matched = true;
                    html += '<option value="' + esc(us[u].code) + '"' + (sel ? ' selected' : '') +
                            '>' + esc(us[u].label) + '</option>';
                }
                html += '</optgroup>';
            }

            // A line carrying a code this build does not know about — written
            // by an older version, or by the API — keeps it, visibly, rather
            // than being silently re-labelled as something else the moment
            // somebody opens the quote.
            if (!matched) {
                html += '<optgroup label="On this line"><option value="' + esc(chosen) +
                        '" selected>' + esc(chosen) + '</option></optgroup>';
            }

            return html + '</select>';
        }

        // ── 055: discount mode ───────────────────────────────────────
        function isPct(r) {
            return r.discountPercent !== null && r.discountPercent !== undefined;
        }

        /// What the single discount box shows: the percentage in % mode,
        /// the amount otherwise.
        function discountInputValue(r) {
            return isPct(r) ? r.discountPercent : num(r.lineDiscount, 0);
        }

        function discountModeSelect(k, r, lineNo) {
            var pct = isPct(r);
            return '<select class="form-select form-select-sm qe-dmode' + (pct ? ' pct' : '') + '"' +
                   ' id="qe-dmode-' + k + '" data-key="' + k + '" data-f="discountMode"' +
                   ' aria-label="Discount is an amount or a percentage, line ' + lineNo + '">' +
                   '<option value="amt"' + (pct ? '' : ' selected') + '>' + esc(CCY) + '</option>' +
                   '<option value="pct"' + (pct ? ' selected' : '') + '>%</option>' +
                   '</select>';
        }

        /// Switching mode CONVERTS. Flipping to % to see what a figure is
        /// worth, then flipping back, must not wipe what was typed — and a
        /// reset there would be silent, because the box is repainted anyway.
        function setDiscountMode(r, mode) {
            if (mode === 'pct') {
                if (isPct(r)) return;
                var sub = lineSubtotal(r);
                r.discountPercent = sub > 0
                    ? Math.round(num(r.lineDiscount, 0) / sub * 100 * 100) / 100
                    : 0;
                if (r.discountPercent > 100) r.discountPercent = 100;
            } else {
                if (!isPct(r)) return;
                r.lineDiscount = rawDiscount(r);   // freeze what the % was worth
                r.discountPercent = null;
            }
        }

        // ── the model ────────────────────────────────────────────────
        function blank() {
            return {
                key: uid++, itemId: null, productId: null,
                name: '', description: '',
                quantity: 1, unitOfMeasure: DEFAULT_UNIT,
                unitPrice: 0, lineDiscount: 0,
                discountPercent: null,          // 055: null = typed as an amount
                taxRate: num(DEFAULT_TAX, 0),
                taxCode: '',                    // 067: '' = no classification
                listPrice: 0
            };
        }

        function seed() {
            if (Array.isArray(SEED)) {
                SEED.forEach(function (s) {
                    var pid = s.productId || null;
                    rows.push({
                        key: uid++,
                        itemId: s.itemId || null,
                        productId: pid,
                        name: s.name || '',
                        description: s.description || '',
                        quantity: num(s.quantity, 1),
                        // 052. A quote written before this round has no unit
                        // in its seed — fall back rather than render a blank
                        // dropdown.
                        unitOfMeasure: s.unitOfMeasure || DEFAULT_UNIT,
                        unitPrice: num(s.unitPrice, 0),
                        lineDiscount: num(s.lineDiscount, 0),
                        // 055. null, not 0: "discounted by a round number" and
                        // "not discounted" have to stay distinguishable.
                        discountPercent: (s.discountPercent === null ||
                                          s.discountPercent === undefined ||
                                          s.discountPercent === '')
                            ? null : num(s.discountPercent, 0),
                        // num(), NOT asPercent(). The seed is ALREADY a
                        // percentage — Edit.cshtml multiplies the DTO's fraction
                        // by 100 before serialising. Running asPercent() over it
                        // again would turn a genuine 0.5% rate into 50%, because
                        // asPercent treats anything in (0,1] as a fraction.
                        taxRate: num(s.taxRate, num(DEFAULT_TAX, 0)),
                        // 067. A quote written before this round has no code
                        // in its seed, and neither has a line in a market
                        // that asks for none. '' is the right answer for both
                        // — and it is what gets posted back, which the server
                        // reads as "deliberately empty" rather than "say
                        // nothing and let the product decide". That is what
                        // lets a rep CLEAR a code the catalogue supplied.
                        taxCode: (s.taxCode === null || s.taxCode === undefined)
                            ? '' : String(s.taxCode),
                        listPrice: (pid && LIST_PRICES && LIST_PRICES[pid] != null)
                            ? num(LIST_PRICES[pid], 0) : num(s.unitPrice, 0)
                    });
                });
            }
            if (rows.length === 0 && SEED_BLANK) rows.push(blank());
        }

        // ── maths, in ONE place ──────────────────────────────────────
        // Every caller uses these, so the Discount row, the line totals, the
        // grand total and the approval hint can never disagree.
        function lineSubtotal(r) { return Math.max(0, num(r.quantity, 0)) * Math.max(0, num(r.unitPrice, 0)); }

        /// 055. The discount AMOUNT for a row, whichever way it was typed.
        /// In % mode the stored amount is derived here and nowhere else, so
        /// the line total, the Discount row, the approval hint and what gets
        /// posted are all the same number by construction.
        function rawDiscount(r) {
            if (r.discountPercent === null || r.discountPercent === undefined)
                return num(r.lineDiscount, 0);

            var pct = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, num(r.discountPercent, 0)));
            return round2(lineSubtotal(r) * pct / 100);
        }

        /// Money, to the currency's places. Matches LineDiscounts.AmountFrom
        /// on the server — half-up, two places — so the figure shown and the
        /// figure stored agree to the cent.
        function round2(x) {
            return Math.round((num(x, 0) + Number.EPSILON) * 100) / 100;
        }

        /// Discount actually applied — never more than the line is worth.
        function lineDiscount(r) {
            return Math.min(Math.max(0, rawDiscount(r)), lineSubtotal(r));
        }

        function lineNet(r)   { return lineSubtotal(r) - lineDiscount(r); }
        function lineTax(r)   { return lineNet(r) * (Math.max(0, num(r.taxRate, 0)) / 100); }
        function lineTotal(r) { return lineNet(r) + lineTax(r); }

        /// Percentage off the reference price, which is the catalogue list
        /// price when there is one and the entered unit price otherwise.
        /// Same shape as the server's rule.
        function discountPct(r) {
            var qty = Math.max(0, num(r.quantity, 0));
            var ref = (num(r.listPrice, 0) > 0 ? num(r.listPrice, 0) : num(r.unitPrice, 0)) * qty;
            if (ref <= 0) return 0;
            var pct = (ref - lineNet(r)) / ref * 100;
            return pct > 0 ? pct : 0;
        }

        // ── render ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
        function esc(s) {
            return String(s == null ? '' : s)
                .split('&').join('&amp;')
                .split('<').join('&lt;')
                .split('>').join('&gt;')
                .split('"').join('&quot;')
                .split("'").join('&#39;');
        }

        function render() {
            if (rows.length === 0) {
                body.innerHTML = '';
                if (emptyEl) emptyEl.classList.remove('d-none');
                recalc();
                return;
            }
            if (emptyEl) emptyEl.classList.add('d-none');

            var html = '';
            for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                var r = rows[i];
                var k = r.key;
                html +=
                '<tr data-key="' + k + '">' +
                  '<td class="qe-row-no">' + (i + 1) + '</td>' +
                  '<td data-lbl="Item">' +
                    '<input type="text" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="qe-name-' + k + '"' +
                      ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="name" value="' + esc(r.name) + '"' +
                      ' placeholder="What are you selling?" maxlength="200"' +
                      ' aria-label="Item name, line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                    // 067. Description and tax code share a row. The code is
                    // optional everywhere and most workspaces will leave it
                    // alone, so it is quiet rather than absent: a line on an
                    // Indian GST invoice has to carry one, and a custom line
                    // typed by hand has no product to inherit it from — which
                    // is exactly the case a product-only snapshot misses.
                    '<div class="qe-item-row">' +
                      '<div class="qe-desc-wrap">' +
                        '<input type="text" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="qe-desc-' + k + '"' +
                          ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="description" value="' + esc(r.description) + '"' +
                          ' placeholder="Description (optional)" maxlength="500"' +
                          ' aria-label="Description, line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                      '</div>' +
                      '<input type="text" class="form-control form-control-sm qe-taxcode"' +
                        ' id="qe-taxcode-' + k + '"' +
                        ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="taxCode" value="' + esc(r.taxCode) + '"' +
                        ' placeholder="' + esc(TAX_CODE_LABEL) + '" maxlength="' + TAX_CODE_MAX + '"' +
                        ' title="' + esc(TAX_CODE_LABEL) + ' for this line. Optional — printed on the quote and the invoice when set."' +
                        ' aria-label="' + esc(TAX_CODE_LABEL) + ', line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                    '</div>' +
                  '</td>' +
                  '<td data-lbl="Qty">' +
                    // 052. step="any", not step="0.0001". With a step set, the
                    // browser rejects any value not on the step grid with its
                    // own bubble — and because the host page's buttons are
                    // type="submit", that bubble suppresses the submit event,
                    // so THIS editor's message never appears and the two
                    // compete. Same reasoning as the discount input's missing
                    // max=, a few lines down in recalc().
                    '<input type="number" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="qe-qty-' + k + '"' +
                      ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="quantity" value="' + r.quantity + '"' +
                      ' min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal"' +
                      ' aria-label="Quantity, line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                    unitSelect(k, r.unitOfMeasure, i + 1) +
                  '</td>' +
                  '<td data-lbl="Unit price">' +
                    '<input type="number" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="qe-price-' + k + '"' +
                      ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="unitPrice" value="' + r.unitPrice + '"' +
                      ' min="0" step="0.01" aria-label="Unit price, line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                  '</td>' +
                  '<td data-lbl="Discount">' +
                    // 055. ONE box, whose meaning follows the selector under
                    // it. Two boxes would let a line carry both a percentage
                    // and an unrelated amount, and the server would have to
                    // pick one — which is exactly the ambiguity the single
                    // stored amount avoids.
                    '<input type="number" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="qe-disc-' + k + '"' +
                      ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="discountInput" value="' + discountInputValue(r) + '"' +
                      ' min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal"' +
                      ' aria-label="Discount ' + (isPct(r) ? 'percentage' : 'amount') +
                      ', line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                    discountModeSelect(k, r, i + 1) +
                    '<span class="qe-pct" id="qe-pct-' + k + '"></span>' +
                  '</td>' +
                  '<td data-lbl="Tax %">' +
                    '<input type="number" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="qe-tax-' + k + '"' +
                      ' data-key="' + k + '" data-f="taxRate" value="' + r.taxRate + '"' +
                      ' min="0" max="100" step="0.01" aria-label="Tax percent, line ' + (i + 1) + '" />' +
                  '</td>' +
                  '<td class="qe-line-total qe-n" data-lbl="Line total" id="qe-total-' + k + '"></td>' +
                  '<td class="qe-n">' +
                    '<button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger qe-rm" data-rm="' + k + '"' +
                      ' title="Remove line ' + (i + 1) + '" aria-label="Remove line ' + (i + 1) + '">' +
                      '<i class="bi bi-trash"></i></button>' +
                  '</td>' +
                '</tr>';
            }
            body.innerHTML = html;
            recalc();
        }

        function rowByKey(k) {
            for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) if (rows[i].key === k) return rows[i];
            return null;
        }

        // ── recalc ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
        function recalc() {
            var sub = 0, disc = 0, tax = 0;

            for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                var r = rows[i];
                sub  += lineSubtotal(r);
                disc += lineDiscount(r);
                tax  += lineTax(r);

                var tEl = document.getElementById('qe-total-' + r.key);
                if (tEl) tEl.textContent = money(lineTotal(r));

                // Deliberately NOT setting a max= on the discount input. The
                // buttons are type="submit", so a max= the user exceeds makes
                // the browser block the post with its own native bubble — and
                // the submit event never fires, so this editor's own message
                // never appears and the two compete. validate() catches it and
                // says which line, which the native bubble cannot.

                var pEl = document.getElementById('qe-pct-' + r.key);
                if (pEl) {
                    // 055. In % mode, show what the percentage is WORTH —
                    // that is the number going on the customer's document,
                    // and a rep agreeing a discount should see it before
                    // they save, not after. In amount mode this stays what
                    // it always was: how far below list the line has been
                    // cut, which is what the approval rules measure.
                    if (isPct(r)) {
                        var amt = lineDiscount(r);
                        pEl.textContent = amt > 0 ? ('= ' + money(amt)) : '';
                    } else {
                        var pct = discountPct(r);
                        pEl.textContent = pct > 0 ? ('−' + pct.toFixed(1) + '%') : '';
                    }
                }
            }

            var grand = sub - disc + tax;

            set('qeSubtotal', money(sub));
            set('qeDiscount', disc > 0 ? '−' + money(disc) : money(0));
            set('qeTax', money(tax));
            set('qeGrand', money(grand));

            hint(grand);
        }

        function set(id, text) {
            var el = document.getElementById(id);
            if (el) el.textContent = text;
        }

        // ── approval hint ────────────────────────────────────────────
        function hint(grand) {
            var box   = document.getElementById('qeHint');
            var list  = document.getElementById('qeHintList');
            var title = document.getElementById('qeHintTitle');
            var foot  = document.getElementById('qeHintFoot');
            if (!box || !list) return;

            var reasons = [];
            var over = {};

            if (RULES && RULES.enabled) {
                var limit = RULES.maxDiscountPercent;
                if (limit !== null && limit !== undefined) {
                    for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                        var pct = discountPct(rows[i]);
                        if (pct > limit + 0.0001) {
                            over[rows[i].key] = true;
                            reasons.push('"' + esc(rows[i].name || 'Unnamed line') + '" is ' +
                                         pct.toFixed(1) + '% below list price (limit ' + limit + '%).');
                        }
                    }
                }
                var maxTotal = RULES.maxQuoteTotal;
                if (maxTotal !== null && maxTotal !== undefined && grand > maxTotal) {
                    reasons.push('The total ' + money(grand) + ' is above the ' + money(maxTotal) + ' limit.');
                }
            }

            for (var j = 0; j < rows.length; j++) {
                var tr = body.querySelector('tr[data-key="' + rows[j].key + '"]');
                if (tr) tr.classList.toggle('qe-over', !!over[rows[j].key]);
                var pEl = document.getElementById('qe-pct-' + rows[j].key);
                if (pEl) pEl.classList.toggle('over', !!over[rows[j].key]);
            }

            var needs  = reasons.length > 0;
            var exempt = !!(RULES && RULES.exempt);

            box.classList.toggle('d-none', !needs);
            list.innerHTML = reasons.map(function (r) { return '<li>' + r + '</li>'; }).join('');

            if (title) title.textContent = exempt
                ? "Over your workspace's limits"
                : 'This quote will need approval before it can be sent';
            if (foot) foot.textContent = exempt
                ? "You're a workspace admin, so you can still send it yourself."
                : 'You can still save it as a draft. Submitting it for approval sends it to whoever your workspace’s rules name.';

            // Tell the host page, so it can relabel its primary button. Nothing
            // here reaches into the page's own markup.
            document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('quote-items:approval', {
                detail: { needsApproval: needs, exempt: exempt, grandTotal: grand, reasons: reasons }
            }));
        }

        // ── read the DOM back into the model ─────────────────────────
        // The old pages copied only name and description out of the DOM and
        // trusted oninput for the four numbers. Read all six, every time.
        function syncFromDom() {
            for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                var r = rows[i], k = r.key;
                var n = document.getElementById('qe-name-' + k);
                var d = document.getElementById('qe-desc-' + k);
                var q = document.getElementById('qe-qty-' + k);
                var u = document.getElementById('qe-uom-' + k);
                var p = document.getElementById('qe-price-' + k);
                var c = document.getElementById('qe-disc-' + k);
                var m = document.getElementById('qe-dmode-' + k);   // 055
                var t = document.getElementById('qe-tax-' + k);
                var x = document.getElementById('qe-taxcode-' + k); // 067

                if (n) r.name         = n.value || '';
                if (d) r.description  = d.value || '';
                if (q) r.quantity     = qty(q.value, 0);
                if (u) r.unitOfMeasure = u.value || DEFAULT_UNIT;
                if (p) r.unitPrice    = num(p.value, 0);
                // 055. Mode FIRST — it decides what the box beside it means.
                // Reading the number first would file a percentage as an
                // amount on any path where both changed at once.
                if (m) setDiscountMode(r, m.value === 'pct' ? 'pct' : 'amt');
                if (c) {
                    if (isPct(r)) r.discountPercent = num(c.value, 0);
                    else          r.lineDiscount    = num(c.value, 0);
                }
                if (t) r.taxRate      = num(t.value, 0);
                // 067. A string, trimmed here so what is validated, what is
                // shown and what is posted are the same value. Never num().
                if (x) r.taxCode      = (x.value || '').trim();
            }
        }

        function mark(id, bad) {
            var el = document.getElementById(id);
            if (el) el.classList.toggle('is-invalid', !!bad);
        }

        /// Returns a list of problems, and marks the cells. Empty means OK.
        function validate() {
            var problems = [];

            for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                var r = rows[i], k = r.key, n = i + 1;

                var noName = !r.name || !r.name.trim();
                mark('qe-name-' + k, noName);
                if (noName) problems.push('Line ' + n + ' has no item name.');

                // 052. Was: at least 1, and a whole number. Both parts had to
                // go — 0.5 days and 12.5 m² are the reason this round exists.
                // What is left is the one rule that still holds: a line has to
                // be for SOMETHING.
                var badQty = !(r.quantity > 0);
                mark('qe-qty-' + k, badQty);
                if (badQty) problems.push('Line ' + n + ' needs a quantity above zero.');

                var badPrice = !(r.unitPrice > 0);
                mark('qe-price-' + k, badPrice);
                if (badPrice) problems.push('Line ' + n + ' needs a unit price above zero.');

                var badTax = !(r.taxRate >= 0 && r.taxRate <= 100);
                mark('qe-tax-' + k, badTax);
                if (badTax) problems.push('Line ' + n + ' has a tax rate outside 0–100%.');

                // 055. In % mode the rule is 0–100 and the amount cannot
                // exceed the line by construction; in amount mode it is the
                // rule it always was. LineDiscounts.Resolve enforces the same
                // two on the server.
                var sub = lineSubtotal(r);
                var badDisc = false;

                if (isPct(r)) {
                    var p = num(r.discountPercent, 0);
                    badDisc = p < 0 || p > 100;
                    if (badDisc) problems.push(p < 0
                        ? 'Line ' + n + ' has a negative discount percentage.'
                        : 'Line ' + n + ' has a discount above 100%.');
                } else {
                    var amt = num(r.lineDiscount, 0);
                    badDisc = amt < 0 || amt > sub + 0.0001;
                    if (badDisc) problems.push(amt < 0
                        ? 'Line ' + n + ' has a negative discount.'
                        : 'Line ' + n + ' has a discount larger than the line itself (' + money(sub) + ').');
                }
                mark('qe-disc-' + k, badDisc);
            }

            if (rows.length === 0) problems.push('A quote needs at least one line.');
            return problems;
        }

        function showProblems(problems) {
            var box  = document.getElementById('qeProblems');
            var list = document.getElementById('qeProblemList');
            if (!box || !list) return;

            if (problems.length === 0) { box.classList.add('d-none'); return; }

            list.innerHTML = problems.map(function (p) { return '<li>' + esc(p) + '</li>'; }).join('');
            box.classList.remove('d-none');
            box.scrollIntoView({ block: 'center', behavior: 'smooth' });

            var firstBad = body.querySelector('.is-invalid');
            if (firstBad) firstBad.focus({ preventScroll: true });
        }

        // ── the public bit the host page calls ───────────────────────
        // Returns true when the hidden field has been filled and the form may
        // be submitted; false when there is something to fix.
        window.QuoteItemsEditor = {
            prepare: function () {
                syncFromDom();
                recalc();

                var problems = validate();
                showProblems(problems);
                if (problems.length > 0) return false;

                jsonEl.value = JSON.stringify(rows.map(function (r) {
                    return {
                        // The server's QuoteItemData.Id is a Guid? — an existing
                        // line's DB id, or null for a new one. `key` is a DOM
                        // counter and must never be sent: Create's old code sent
                        // item.dbId, which nothing ever set.
                        id: r.itemId || null,
                        productId: r.productId || null,
                        name: (r.name || '').trim(),
                        description: (r.description || '').trim(),
                        quantity: qty(r.quantity, 0),
                        unitOfMeasure: r.unitOfMeasure || DEFAULT_UNIT,
                        unitPrice: r.unitPrice,
                        // 055. Both go. The server recomputes the amount from
                        // the percentage and ignores this one when a percentage
                        // is present — LineDiscounts.Resolve. This is what the
                        // totals on screen were built from, so the two agree.
                        lineDiscount: lineDiscount(r),   // clamped, as displayed
                        discountPercent: isPct(r)
                            ? Math.round(num(r.discountPercent, 0) * 100) / 100
                            : null,
                        taxRate: r.taxRate,              // percentage; the server divides by 100
                        // 067. Always sent, even empty. "" and null mean
                        // DIFFERENT things to LineTaxCodes.Resolve: "" is
                        // "this line has no classification, leave it alone",
                        // null is "I have nothing to say, ask the product".
                        // This editor always has something to say, so it
                        // always sends a string.
                        taxCode: (r.taxCode || '').trim()
                    };
                }));
                return true;
            },
            count: function () { return rows.length; }
        };

        // ── events ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
        body.addEventListener('input', function (e) {
            var el = e.target;
            if (!el || !el.getAttribute) return;
            var f = el.getAttribute('data-f');
            var k = parseInt(el.getAttribute('data-key'), 10);
            if (!f || !Number.isFinite(k)) return;

            var r = rowByKey(k);
            if (!r) return;

            if (f === 'name' || f === 'description') {
                r[f] = el.value || '';
                if (f === 'name' && el.value.trim()) el.classList.remove('is-invalid');
            } else if (f === 'unitOfMeasure') {
                // 052. A string, not a number. Without this branch the unit
                // select would fall into num() below and every change would
                // store 0 — and the line would post a unit of "0".
                r[f] = el.value || DEFAULT_UNIT;
            } else if (f === 'taxCode') {
                // 067. Also a string. Same trap as the unit: without this
                // branch an HSN code would go through num() and every line
                // would post a tax code of "0" — or of "998314" read as a
                // number, which is the same bug wearing a hat.
                //
                // NOT trimmed here. Trimming on every keystroke would stop
                // somebody typing a space, and syncFromDom trims before
                // anything is validated or posted.
                r[f] = el.value || '';
            } else if (f === 'quantity') {
                r[f] = qty(el.value, 0);
                el.classList.remove('is-invalid');
            } else if (f === 'discountMode') {
                // 055. A repaint, not an assignment: the box beside this
                // selector now means something else, so its value has to be
                // rewritten. Only this row is touched.
                setDiscountMode(r, el.value === 'pct' ? 'pct' : 'amt');
                var box = document.getElementById('qe-disc-' + k);
                if (box) box.value = discountInputValue(r);
                el.classList.toggle('pct', isPct(r));
            } else if (f === 'discountInput') {
                if (isPct(r)) r.discountPercent = num(el.value, 0);
                else          r.lineDiscount    = num(el.value, 0);
                el.classList.remove('is-invalid');
            } else {
                r[f] = num(el.value, 0);
                el.classList.remove('is-invalid');
            }
            recalc();
        });

        body.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            var btn = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('[data-rm]') : null;
            if (!btn) return;
            var k = parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-rm'), 10);
            // Read the DOM first: re-rendering throws the inputs away, so
            // anything typed into another line and not yet echoed into the
            // model would be lost when a line is removed.
            syncFromDom();
            rows = rows.filter(function (r) { return r.key !== k; });
            render();
        });

        var addBtn = document.getElementById('qeAddLine');
        if (addBtn) addBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
            syncFromDom();
            rows.push(blank());
            render();
            var last = rows[rows.length - 1];
            var el = document.getElementById('qe-name-' + last.key);
            if (el) el.focus();
        });

        // ── catalogue ────────────────────────────────────────────────
        var openBtn = document.getElementById('qeOpenCatalog');
        var catalog = document.getElementById('qeCatalog');

        if (openBtn) openBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
            if (!catalog || typeof bootstrap === 'undefined') {
                // Don't fail silently the way the old page did — say so.
                window.alert('The catalogue needs JavaScript from the page layout to open. Add the line by hand instead.');
                return;
            }
            bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(catalog).show();
        });

        if (catalog) {
            catalog.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                var b = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.qe-prod') : null;
                if (!b) return;

                syncFromDom();

                // ── 069: EMPTY IS NOT ZERO, AGAIN ────────────────────
                //
                // The same distinction the tax rate needed in 050, for a
                // sharper reason. An empty data-price means this product
                // has no price in the quote's currency; a "0" means it is
                // genuinely free. num('', 0) and num('0', 0) are
                // indistinguishable, so the raw attribute is tested.
                //
                // Both end up at 0 on the line — but only the empty case
                // leaves listPrice at 0 too, which keeps the discount
                // maths from measuring against a price that does not
                // exist, and the rep has to type a figure before the
                // editor will let the quote save.
                var rawPrice = b.getAttribute('data-price');
                var hasPrice = !(rawPrice === null || rawPrice === '');
                var price    = hasPrice ? num(rawPrice, 0) : 0;

                // ── 070: A BUNDLE BECOMES **ONE** LINE ───────────────
                //
                // Not one line per component. The customer sees a price
                // they can say yes to, and nothing in the line maths,
                // the tax maths, the approval rules, the PDF layout or
                // CreateInvoiceFromQuoteHandler has to change — a bundle
                // line is an ordinary line with a longer description.
                //
                // The contents go into the DESCRIPTION, and that is the
                // snapshot: the sentence is frozen here, at the moment
                // the line is added, so a quote already sent never
                // changes when somebody edits the bundle. The bundle
                // itself stays a live reference everywhere else.
                // Definition live, document frozen.
                //
                // It is APPENDED to the product's own description rather
                // than replacing it, because a bundle can have both — a
                // sentence about what the package is for, and then what
                // is in it.
                //
                // WORTH KNOWING: the line carries ONE tax rate and ONE
                // tax code, taken from the bundle product itself. A
                // bundle mixing 5% goods with 18% services cannot be
                // quoted as a single line under Indian GST; the product
                // form says so, and the answer is to quote those
                // components separately.
                var ownDesc  = b.getAttribute('data-desc') || '';
                var bundleOf = b.getAttribute('data-bundle') || '';

                var description = bundleOf
                    ? (ownDesc ? ownDesc + ' — ' + bundleOf : bundleOf)
                    : ownDesc;

                // QuoteItem.Description is NVARCHAR(500) and this input
                // carries maxlength="500" — which restricts TYPING and
                // not a value set by script. ProductBundles caps the
                // breakdown at 460, but a bundle whose product ALSO has a
                // description of its own can push the pair over.
                //
                // Cut here rather than letting SQL Server do it silently.
                // An ellipsis on screen is something a rep can see and
                // shorten; a description that lost its last component
                // between the browser and the database is not.
                if (description.length > 500) {
                    description = description.slice(0, 499) + '\u2026';
                }

                // ── 050: the product's OWN tax rate ──────────────────
                //
                // This line used to read `taxRate: num(DEFAULT_TAX, 0)`,
                // so the rate set on a product was never used — pick a 5%
                // product in a 7% workspace and the line came out at 7%.
                // Product.TaxRate was decorative, and the quote (and the
                // invoice raised from it) were quietly wrong for anyone
                // who had set one.
                //
                // EMPTY IS NOT ZERO, and the difference matters: a product
                // with no rate set should inherit the workspace default,
                // while a product deliberately set to 0 is tax-exempt and
                // must STAY at 0. Testing the raw attribute for '' rather
                // than testing the parsed number for falsiness is what
                // keeps those apart — num('', x) and num('0', x) both look
                // like "nothing" to a truthiness check.
                var rawTax = b.getAttribute('data-tax');
                var taxRate = (rawTax === null || rawTax === '')
                    ? num(DEFAULT_TAX, 0)
                    : num(rawTax, num(DEFAULT_TAX, 0));

                rows.push({
                    key: uid++, itemId: null,
                    productId: b.getAttribute('data-id') || null,
                    name: b.getAttribute('data-name') || '',
                    // 070. The product's description plus, for a bundle,
                    // what is in it. See the note above.
                    description: description,
                    quantity: 1,
                    // 052. The product's own unit, snapshotted now. A line
                    // added from the catalogue should not need the unit picked
                    // by hand — the catalogue already knows.
                    unitOfMeasure: b.getAttribute('data-unit') || DEFAULT_UNIT,
                    unitPrice: price,
                    lineDiscount: 0,
                    discountPercent: null,   // 055

                    taxRate: taxRate,

                    // ── 067: the product's own classification code ───────
                    //
                    // Snapshotted here, exactly like the unit above, so a
                    // line added from the catalogue arrives with its HSN /
                    // SAC already filled in and the rep does not retype it
                    // on every quote.
                    //
                    // '' for a product with no code, which is the honest
                    // answer and the one the server reads as "no
                    // classification on this line". There is no empty-vs-zero
                    // trap here the way there is for the tax RATE — a code
                    // is a string, and an absent one has only one meaning.
                    taxCode: (b.getAttribute('data-taxcode') || '').trim(),

                    // 069. ZERO when there is no price in this currency,
                    // so the "how far below list is this line" maths does
                    // not measure against a figure that was never a price
                    // in the quote's currency. See hasPrice above.
                    listPrice: hasPrice ? price : 0
                });
                render();

                if (typeof bootstrap !== 'undefined') {
                    bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(catalog).hide();
                }
            });

            var search = document.getElementById('qeProdSearch');
            if (search) search.addEventListener('input', function () {
                var term = (search.value || '').trim().toLowerCase();
                var items = catalog.querySelectorAll('.qe-prod');
                var shown = 0;
                for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
                    var hit = term === '' || (items[i].textContent || '').toLowerCase().indexOf(term) !== -1;
                    items[i].classList.toggle('d-none', !hit);
                    if (hit) shown++;
                }
                var none = document.getElementById('qeProdNone');
                if (none) none.classList.toggle('d-none', shown !== 0);
            });
        }

        // ── the form's submit event is the ONLY path ─────────────────
        // The old pages had onclick="submitQuote(true)" calling
        // form.submit(), which skips constraint validation AND the submit
        // event. The host page's buttons are plain type="submit" now, so the
        // browser validates, this listener serialises the lines, and Enter in
        // a text box behaves like everything else.
        var form = document.getElementById(FORM_ID);
        if (form) {
            form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
                if (!window.QuoteItemsEditor.prepare()) e.preventDefault();
            });
        } else if (window.console && console.warn) {
            console.warn('_QuoteItemsEditor: no form with id "' + FORM_ID +
                         '" — line items will not be submitted.');
        }

        // ── first paint ──────────────────────────────────────────────
        // Deferred to DOMContentLoaded on purpose. window.MerkaiCurrency is
        // defined by _Layout in a script near the end of <body>, which has not
        // run yet while this partial is being parsed. Calling money() now would
        // fall through to toFixed(2) and the opening totals would render
        // ungrouped ("255000.00") until the first keystroke redrew them.
        function start() { seed(); render(); }

        if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
            document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', start);
        } else {
            start();
        }
    })();
</script>
